# =========================================================
# MA et al. PCL/CALB REACTION-DIFFUSION MODEL
# MANUSCRIPT-ALIGNED TWO-VARIANT IMPLEMENTATION + COMBINED PLOTS
# Redraw saved comparisons without refitting:
# runfile('MA_IWA_NIWA_DEGRADED_FRACTION_SVG_FIXED.py', args='--combined-plots-only')
# =========================================================
# Supervisor-approved manuscript variants:
#   IWA  = inhibition with amorphisation
#   NIWA = no inhibition with amorphisation
#
# Common irreversible network:
#   E + C  --k1-->  ZC
#   ZC     --kc-->  E + D
#   ZC     --kr-->  E + A              [present in both retained variants]
#   E + A  --k4-->  ZA
#   ZA     --ka-->  E + D
#   D      --ke-->  P
#   E + P  --ki-->  ZI                 [IWA only]
#
# Free released product P(t) is a single well-mixed scalar state:
#   dP/dt = mean(ke D)/S0 - mean(ki E P)     with inhibition
#   dP/dt = mean(ke D)/S0                    without inhibition
#
# Bath pH is predicted from P(t), not imposed:
#   pH(t) = pH0 - alpha_pH P(t)
#
# Pore-gated enzyme transport:
#   phi = 1 - (C + A + ZC + ZA + D)/S0
#   D_E(phi) = De0 * phi
#   D_E(0) = 0 in intact polymer.
#
# Fitting:
#   ordinary simultaneous (joint) least squares with NO scaling and NO weighting:
#       r_WL = WL_pred - WL_obs
#       r_Xc = Xc_pred - Xc_obs
#       r_pH = pH_pred - pH_obs
#   All residuals enter the objective directly in their native numerical units.
#   Positive parameters are optimized in logarithmic coordinates.
#   Local bounded least-squares (TRF) is used directly in log-space.
#   No PSO/global optimiser is used.
#
# Model selection:
#   All 9 WL + 9 Xc + 9 pH observations are retained: n = 27.
#   AIC/AICc are computed from the SAME raw joint residual SSE minimized
#   during fitting. K = p + 1, where p is the number of mechanistic
#   parameters and +1 is the estimated common residual-variance parameter.
#   Models are ranked by AICc because n is small relative to K.
# =========================================================

